    "As of 9 November the filing's figures are updated and much larger. Amendment No. 1 to Anthropic's Form S-1, filed 2 November, reports revenue of $17.0 billion for the three months ended September 30, 2026 against an operating loss of $567 million, and purchase commitments and leases with \"an aggregate committed spend of approximately $895.4 billion, substantially all of which is related to compute and infrastructure\", of which approximately $69.8 billion falls due in the 12 months after 30 September. Data Center Dynamics reads the prospectus as committing \"$121.3bn to lease compute from Google, $120.5bn from SpaceX, $110bn from Amazon, and $44.9bn from Microsoft\", and puts quarter-on-quarter revenue growth at 47 percent against 144 percent in the second quarter. TechCrunch reads compute at 58% of revenue, up from 48%, on a $10 billion quarterly bill. TeraWulf said Google executed credit support agreements behind debt financing supporting approximately $19 billion of Anthropic lease commitments in Hawesville, Kentucky, and CNBC, citing the Financial Times, reported Anthropic paying about $3.4 billion for commitments to 1.7 gigawatts of gas generators.",
    "The pricing half of the question moved against both labs in the same week. Reuters reported investors raising doubts about whether Anthropic can hold its roadshow in time for a November listing, with some viewing the discussed US$1.5-trillion valuation as at the high end of expectations, and the filing leaves October revenue blank. TechCrunch reported OpenAI raising $11 billion at a $1.25 trillion valuation, against the $30 billion Bloomberg reported in late September that it was seeking. On 5 November CNN reported a rout that \"wiped out roughly $2.5 trillion in market value\", with the Nasdaq 100 down 6.36% and Nvidia down 9.3%; Taiwan's Taiex fell 1,873.08 points the next day. CNBC reported Microsoft shrinking its neocloud roster and declining to renew a deal with Oracle, and Ramp card data showed corporate token spend growing 1.5% across August and September. No developer disclosed a change to its capital plans."
